The account-wide reputation pool no longer crosses the faction line, and the
damage it wrote during its first days alive is repaired by migration.

Touches: modules/mod-living-gear/src/LivingGear_Next.cpp (gitignored module
         edit -- RepTeamLegalTeams/RepWorstBaseFor/RepTeamBitFor helpers plus
         four gates: capture, propagate, login backfill, login replay)
         data/sql/updates/pending_db_characters/rev_reputation_team_scope.sql
         (pending migration; imported with the next ship)
No tracked src/server/ files change.

Why: report #220 -- "Most of my characters are Alliance so when I logged
into a Horde character, it set all my reputations to Alliance-levels (so
negative). Need to have that reversed and only have reputations share
faction-wide maybe?"

Mechanics of the bug: Faction.dbc gives every faction race-dependent base
reputation, and every one-team faction (the nine cities, the BG teams, the
expedition factions, Kurenai vs The Mag'har, ...) puts each character of the
OPPOSITE team at Hated (-42000) through a base-reputation slot covering that
team's races. The pool stores DISPLAYED totals (standing + base), so a value
captured from one team carries that team's base inside it. Replaying it onto
a character of the other team writes raw = total - base(other team): the
account's Alliance characters' Hated Silvermoon (-32110 displayed) landed on
the blood-elf alt as raw -36110 (her base with Silvermoon is +4000), i.e.
Hated with her own capital. The reverse hop wrote Alliance-city exalted onto
her, and each push/replay round trip through characters with different bases
ratcheted values further (her saved raw -45500 for the Horde umbrella faction
is pool -42000 minus her 3500 blood-elf base -- exact arithmetic
confirmation).

Fix, per the reporter's own suggestion ("only share faction-wide"):
RepTeamLegalTeams(faction) computes, exactly like
ReputationMgr::GetBaseReputation (first matching slot, both wildcard rules),
the worst base reputation any race/class of each team starts the faction
with; a team is legal when that worst base is above the Hated floor. The
nine cities, BG teams, expedition factions and one-team quest factions then
sync ONLY between characters of their own team. Neutral factions share
account-wide unchanged, and factions that start EVERYONE at Hated
(Netherwing, Brood of Nozdormu, Sons of Hodir) have a team-independent base
and stay shareable. The gate sits on all four paths: capture
(PushAccountReputation never stores a standing earned by the wrong team),
live propagate (PropagateAccountReputation skips opposite-team alts), login
backfill (seeding skips factions illegal for the logging-in character) and
login replay (stored values for illegal factions are ignored). Helper is
pure -- no cached state, no new threading exposure.

The migration (validated inside a rolled-back transaction on live data)
repairs what the pool already wrote:
  * opposite-team character_reputation rows deleted outright (9054 + 8683
    rows realm-wide, mostly bot default states the engine recreates at load);
  * own-team rows below neutral floored to 0 (17 horde-side + 2
    alliance-side rows -- no gameplay path drops a character below neutral
    with a faction its own team owns, so every negative is sync damage);
  * the 37 contaminated lg_account_reputation rows for one-team factions
    dropped; the gated backfill re-seeds them from correct-team characters
    at next login.

Players whose own-faction city reputations were damaged start those back at
neutral and regrow them (fast under the realm's reputation perks); enemy-city
standings reset to "never contacted", which is what a fresh character shows.
